is labours. He died in 1617, in the 64th year of his age, and was succeeded as botanical professor by one of his sons. Alpini wrote the following works in Latin:—1. De Medicina Ægyptiorum libri iv. Venice, 1591, 4to; 2. De Plantis Ægypti liber, Venice, 1592, 4to; 3. De Balsamo Dialogus, Venice, 1592, 4to;
